{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/init()"],"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/boundEvents"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/fallback(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/handler()","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/on(_:_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/on(eventNamed:_:)"],"title":"Instance Methods"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ReactorRouter","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ReactorRouter","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ReactorRouter","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13ReactorRouterV","roleHeading":"Structure"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ReactorRouter"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§22.10’s handler is ONE function from an event to one answer, which is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right shape for the wire and the wrong shape for the code. A reactor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registered for three events opens with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event.event"},{"type":"text","text":", and that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"switch is where two defects live. The first is cheap: a misspelled event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binds nothing and is discovered as an event that never fires. The second is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not — it is the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"default:"},{"type":"text","text":" arm that returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".allow"},{"type":"text","text":" on behalf of code that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never ran, which is §22.10 rule 2’s defect relocated into user code where the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rule does not reach it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"A BUILDER RATHER THAN AN ATTRIBUTE","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and §22.14 records why: a Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reactor handler is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"type":"text","text":" closure, and collecting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"type":"text","text":" members by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reflection costs a runtime dependency an SDK should not add to hand out an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute. A builder type-checks the closure against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(ReactorEvent) async throws -> ReactorAnswer"},{"type":"text","text":" at compile time, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stricter than what the reflection would have bought. Kotlin made the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trade for the same reason."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PURE SUGAR."}]},{"type":"text","text":" It opens no connection, consumes no queue, verifies no event,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signs no reply and interprets no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timeout_ms"},{"type":"text","text":"; its output is exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handler the runtime accepts (rule 1)."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Bind one handler per event and let the SDK compose them into the single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/reactorServe(config:transport:handler:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" takes.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/reactorrouter"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"AxiamSDK","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ReactorRouter/on(eventNamed:_:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Bind by NAME, for a reactor whose event list is configuration rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"source.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/reactorrouter\/on(eventnamed:_:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"on"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"eventNamed","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK14ReactorHandlera","kind":"typeIdentifier"